 "intro": "Sarmizegetusa Regia, the Dacian capital in the Orăştie Mountains, summer 106 AD. Decebalus has broken the peace. You are Trajan, who has bridged the Danube in stone.",
 "debrief": "Trajan crossed the Danube on Apollodorus’s great stone bridge and closed in on the Dacian capital with several columns, taking the mountain forts. Ancient and later accounts say the Romans cut the city’s water supply. Sarmizegetusa fell, and Decebalus fled; Roman cavalry caught up with him, but he cut his own throat. The cavalryman’s gravestone survives. Dacia became a province, and its gold paid for Trajan’s Forum and Column. Some details of the siege are uncertain. The other choices are what-ifs.",
